## Prerequisites

### Local Setup
- AWS CLI v2 installed and configured (`aws configure`)
- Docker Desktop installed
- Node.js 18+ installed
- Git installed
- AWS account with appropriate permissions

### AWS Permissions Required
Your AWS IAM user/role needs permissions for:
- EC2 (VPC, Security Groups, Instances)
- RDS (PostgreSQL)
- ECR (Elastic Container Registry)
- ECS (Fargate, Tasks, Services)
- CloudWatch (Logs, Metrics)
- IAM (Roles, Policies)
- ALB (Application Load Balancer)

### Variables to Set
Replace these values throughout the guide:
```bash
AWS_REGION=ap-south-1
AWS_ACCOUNT_ID=$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text)
APP_NAME=rag
ECR_REPO_NAME=rag-app
CLUSTER_NAME=rag-cluster
VPC_CIDR=10.0.0.0/16
PRIVATE_SUBNET_1_CIDR=10.0.1.0/24
PRIVATE_SUBNET_2_CIDR=10.0.2.0/24
PUBLIC_SUBNET_1_CIDR=10.0.10.0/24
PUBLIC_SUBNET_2_CIDR=10.0.11.0/24
```

