## Phase 3: Container Registry & Image Management

### Step 10: Create ECR Repository

```bash
# Create ECR repository
ECR_REPO=$(aws ecr create-repository \
  --repository-name $ECR_REPO_NAME \
  --image-scanning-configuration scanOnPush=true \
  --encryption-configuration encryptionType=AES256 \
  --region $AWS_REGION \
  --query 'repository.repositoryUri' \
  --output text)

echo "ECR Repository: $ECR_REPO"

# Set repository URI variable
REPO_URI=$ECR_REPO
```

### Step 11: Push Docker Image to ECR

```bash
# Get ECR login token
aws ecr get-login-password --region $AWS_REGION | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin $REPO_URI

# Build image with version tag
docker build -t rag-app:v1.0 .

# Tag for ECR
docker tag rag-app:v1.0 $REPO_URI:v1.0
docker tag rag-app:v1.0 $REPO_URI:latest

# Push to ECR
docker push $REPO_URI:v1.0
docker push $REPO_URI:latest

# Verify image in ECR
aws ecr describe-images \
  --repository-name $ECR_REPO_NAME \
  --region $AWS_REGION
```

