## Phase 4: Ollama Deployment

### Option A: Self-Hosted Ollama on EC2

#### Step 12A: Launch EC2 Instance

```bash
# Get latest Ubuntu 22.04 LTS AMI
AMI_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-images \
  --owners 099720109477 \
  --filters "Name=name,Values=ubuntu/images/hvm-ssd/ubuntu-jammy-22.04-amd64-server-*" \
  "Name=state,Values=available" \
  --region $AWS_REGION \
  --query 'Images | sort_by(@, &CreationDate) | [-1].ImageId' \
  --output text)

echo "Ubuntu AMI: $AMI_ID"

# Create EC2 key pair (save the .pem file securely)
aws ec2 create-key-pair \
  --key-name rag-ollama-key \
  --region $AWS_REGION \
  --query 'KeyMaterial' \
  --output text > ~/.ssh/rag-ollama-key.pem

chmod 400 ~/.ssh/rag-ollama-key.pem

# Launch EC2 instance
INSTANCE_ID=$(aws ec2 run-instances \
  --image-id $AMI_ID \
  --instance-type t3.micro \
  --key-name rag-ollama-key \
  --security-group-ids $SG_OLLAMA \
  --subnet-id $PUBLIC_SUBNET_1 \
  --associate-public-ip-address \
  --block-device-mappings 'DeviceName=/dev/sda1,Ebs={VolumeSize=30,VolumeType=gp2,DeleteOnTermination=true}' \
  --region $AWS_REGION \
  --query 'Instances[0].InstanceId' \
  --output text)

echo "Instance ID: $INSTANCE_ID"

# Wait for instance to be running
aws ec2 wait instance-running \
  --instance-ids $INSTANCE_ID \
  --region $AWS_REGION

# Get instance IP addresses
INSTANCE_IP=$(aws ec2 describe-instances \
  --instance-ids $INSTANCE_ID \
  --region $AWS_REGION \
  --query 'Reservations[0].Instances[0].PublicIpAddress' \
  --output text)

INSTANCE_PRIVATE_IP=$(aws ec2 describe-instances \
  --instance-ids $INSTANCE_ID \
  --region $AWS_REGION \
  --query 'Reservations[0].Instances[0].PrivateIpAddress' \
  --output text)

echo "Instance Public IP: $INSTANCE_IP"
echo "Instance Private IP: $INSTANCE_PRIVATE_IP"
```

#### Step 13A: Install Ollama on EC2

```bash
# SSH into the instance
ssh -i ~/.ssh/rag-ollama-key.pem ubuntu@$INSTANCE_IP

# Once connected, run these commands:

# Update system
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# Install Ollama
curl https://ollama.ai/install.sh | sh

# Start Ollama service
sudo systemctl start ollama
sudo systemctl enable ollama

# Verify Ollama is running
curl http://localhost:11434/api/version

# Pull models (this will take several minutes)
ollama pull llama3
ollama pull nomic-embed-text

# Configure Ollama to listen on all interfaces
sudo tee /etc/systemd/system/ollama.service.d/override.conf << EOF
[Service]
Environment="OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0:11434"
EOF

# Restart Ollama service
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart ollama

# Verify Ollama is accessible
curl http://localhost:11434/api/tags

# Exit SSH
exit
```

#### Verify Ollama Connection from Local Machine

```bash
